5|0@fivenightsatfreddys^1438846392#cttce4s:Xtremegamer51$:Fnaf 1 still would be my favorite. It has very good and balanced mechanics in my opinion, and honestly has some of the best atmosphere in my opinion. The only thing I didn't like is how sometimes Bonnie and/or Chica would appear at the door and never leave, that was the only unbalanced mechanic in my opinion, but everything else was great. Fnaf 2 was REALLY bad in my opinion. Other then the story telling in it, everything was just plain out bad. The music box for example was implemented badly. With Foxy in Fnaf 1, you gotta check on him as well, yes, but the mechanic at least isn't like the puppet since with the puppet you gotta check on it every few seconds instead of every once and a while, plus since the Puppet doesn't have mutilple phases before he attacks only adds to how annoying it is. Also the game just felt like a cluster in general. At first I liked how the game had so many animatronics when I first saw the trailer, but when the game came out I noticed how it ended up just being animatronics at your face every few seconds. Not to mention, the animatronics either took along time to go away, or you had to be very fast to not die from them, which was more annoying then scary in my opinion. I couldn't help but rage when ever I got jumpscared in Fnaf 2, compared with Fnaf 1 were I either got scared, or had almost no reaction, since with Fnaf 1 you at least have time to react. With Fnaf 3, it was a huge improvement compared to Fnaf 2 in my opinion,but was still pretty damn unfair tbh. What I mean is that with some of the mechanics, well, it just felt like you couldn't stop what was slowing you down. Playing perfectly with no mistake what so ever? Well you still get a random system error anyways sorry. Not to mention Phantom Foxy was horribly implemented in my opinion. While I will admit he made me jump when he appeared, he is still unfair. He just seems like something that will appear randomly and attack you when ever he feels like it, even if you make no mistake. Phantom Foxy is honestly one of the reasons why I can't beat Nightmare in Fnaf 3, since with the other Phantom Animatronics I'm at least able to deal with them so that they don't give me a system error, but then Phantom Foxy decides to show up and fuck me up. Well that was probably alot more text then it should have been, but I think I made my point lol. 
