14|0@fivenightsatfreddys^1438856044#cttesm9:invaderzz$:When FNaF first came out I didn't think much of it at all. I dismissed it. Second game came out, I made fun of it for having 2 games in 3 months. Over time I began to continuously mock the games, I made fun of the developer for making so many games so fast, accused him of milking. All the cliches. Then one day I was browsing YouTube, I came across a FNaF song remix by BobGmbH. I really liked the song, and this was initially gave me a tiny bit of interest in the series. It's funny how a single video caused a chain of events which led me to me typing this right now. A week later FNaF3 came out. I watched Markiplier play through it out of mild interest and I felt touched by the (good) ending. Something about it, I'm not sure what exactly, made me feel happy and sad at the same time. I knew the basic lore and I understood what it meant, and that's when I stopped making fun of the series. I didn't exactly defend it or keep up with it, but I stopped making fun of it. And then- when FNaF4 was announced, with that first teaser- something in me changed. I'm not sure why but I went into full hype mode. A several days later I bought FNaF1, at long last. That night I turned the lights all off, put in my headphones and played. No guide, nothing. I had never been so terrified. And that's when I realized everything I had said- about how scary the game was, jumpscared are overrated, the game is bad- was incorrect. I was so, so very wrong about everything I had been saying since the very first game had come out, and I had talked about it with my friends. Now I love this series, and I love Scott. Over the past 3 months, this series has become one of my favorites of all time. And that's why when I see people saying the very same insults I used- insulting the games, Scott, what we like- It doesn't really bother me. Because I've been there, I've said those exact same thing before. And I know that they're wrong.
