1|0@fivenightsatfreddys^1438869165#cttjmcc:TheFrodo$:How did you guys first find out? I watched Game Grumps do it, and I thought Night 1 was boring so I quit watching. I decided to give it another try 2 days later, on August 25th. And I'm so glad I did. It immediately struck me as way scarier than any of the other horror games I'd seen. When I first saw Bonnie at the door, my heart skipped a beat. I saw people in the comments discussing how Foxy was gonna get them next episode, so I did some research on the game. I found out about the hidden lore. Now this was when I knew this was gonna last a while. Unsolved mysteries! I thought Golden Freddy did the Bite of 87 because of the easter egg and I wasn't wrong. Anyway, I had to watch every let's player play it, and that's how I found Markiplier! I won the game in a giveaway, beat 20/20/20/20, and had endless discussions with friends on this one game. So the first really affected me in a way no other game has. And listening to the Toreador March just brings back those good times. That's why I asked Gil if it was gonna be in the movie. I wanted to represent us generation fnaf 1 fans. Thanks for reading this wall of text, if you did.
